<Prose title="Support · Ake" description="Get help with Ake, the notch countdown for your Mac." heading="Support">
  <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Include your macOS version and what you expected to happen.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <p>Which Macs and calendars work, and which meeting apps Join opens: see the <a href="/#faq">FAQ</a>.</p>

  <h2>Ake doesn’t show my meetings</h2>
  <p>Check that Ake has access in System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Calendars, and that the calendar is switched on in Ake’s Settings › Calendars (Settings is in the menu under Ake’s menu-bar icon).</p>

  <h2>Start fresh</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Quit Ake from its menu-bar icon.</li>
    <li>Move Ake from Applications to the Trash.</li>
    <li>To remove its settings too, delete the folder <code>~/Library/Containers/com.zincer.ake</code>.</li>
  </ol>
</Prose>
